    "text": "A semicircular wire of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> rotates in uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> about its diameter with angular velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>. If the total resistance of the circuit is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, then the mean power generated per period of rotation is",
